This is an ESP32 sketch that reads an RFID/NFC tag using an RC522 reader and shows a short message on a SSD1306 I²C OLED.
Behavior (exact):

If the scanned tag UID equals E1:4D:90:04 → OLED displays Hello!.

If the scanned tag UID equals 83:36:50:E4 → OLED displays Good morning!.

Any other tag → OLED displays Unknown.
After showing the message the display returns to Ready after 1.5 s. The sketch also prints the scanned UID to Serial (115200) to help you capture UIDs for configuration.

Full wiring (exact pins — follow these; power at 3.3 V)

Critical: Power everything with 3.3 V. The RC522 is not 5 V tolerant. Use a common GND.

RC522 (SPI) → ESP32 DevKitC

RC522 3.3V → ESP32 3V3

RC522 GND → ESP32 GND

RC522 SDA (SS) → ESP32 GPIO 5 ← SS_PIN in code

RC522 SCK → ESP32 GPIO 18 ← SPI clock

RC522 MOSI → ESP32 GPIO 23 ← SPI MOSI

RC522 MISO → ESP32 GPIO 19 ← SPI MISO

RC522 RST → ESP32 GPIO 27 ← RST_PIN in code

RC522 IRQ → leave disconnected (NC)

SSD1306 OLED (I²C) → ESP32

OLED VCC → ESP32 3V3

OLED GND → ESP32 GND

OLED SDA → ESP32 GPIO 21 ← I²C SDA (Wire)

OLED SCL → ESP32 GPIO 22 ← I²C SCL (Wire)